Dreamfall — When the Sky Collapsed V3

(15 seconds — 8K UHD / 24 fps / Hyperreal Surrealism)

Video Summary

A hyperreal cinematic short where the dream world loses its laws of physics.
A young woman floats above Manhattan at dawn as the air turns liquid, gravity reverses, and the city folds upon itself.
Her fall becomes a dance through collapsing light until she awakens softly in bed, bathed in morning glow.
The film condenses serenity, awe, and transcendence into one breathtaking, physics-bending moment.

Format & Visual Parameters

Format: 8K UHD (7680×4320, 2.39:1 aspect ratio)
Color Space: DCI-P3 HDR10, 10-bit depth
Framerate: 24 fps
Tone: Surreal realism with physical precision
Camera: 28 mm lens, f/3.2, 1/500 s, ISO 640, WB 7000 K
