Scene-by-Scene Storyboard
Scene 1 — Still Air Above the City (0–1.5 s)

Camera ascends through golden haze over Manhattan.
The woman floats weightlessly, eyes closed, surrounded by faint dust motes.
Mood: calm before the dream shifts.
Audio: soft low wind, slow heartbeat.

Scene 2 — Gentle Drift (1.5–3 s)

Orbiting close-up; her hair ripples as light moves across her face.
Soft flares caress the skyline reflections.
Mood: awakening in wonder.

Scene 3 — Sky Becomes Liquid (3–4.5 s)

Air ripples like water; the edges of skyscrapers distort.
Her dress waves as though submerged.
Physics: pseudo-fluid transition, Re ≈ 200.
Mood: fascination and unease.

Scene 4 — The City Breathes (4.5–6 s)

Buildings pulse subtly, glass façades ripple outward.
Lighting reflections oscillate as if the city itself inhaled.
Mood: awe, disorientation.

Scene 5 — Weightless Turn (6–7.5 s)

Camera rolls with her; floating dust and debris begin to drift in reverse.
Gravity fades to zero.
Audio: deep hum and faint heartbeat pause.

Scene 6 — Inversion (7.5–9 s)

Manhattan flips overhead; gold becomes cold blue light.
She floats between sky and earth, suspended in silence.
Mood: revelation, surrender.

Scene 7 — Fracture Light (9–10.5 s)

Reality distorts. Space warps
Mood: astonishment, dissolution.

Scene 8 — Descent (10.5–12 s)

She begins to fall slowly, arms open, drifting through bending light and swirling clouds.
Time dilates to half speed.
Mood: serene surrender.

Scene 9 — Impact Dissolve (12–13.5 s)

White-gold flash; her body merges seamlessly with her bed sheets.
Ripples travel through fabric like echoes of the dream.
Mood: calm return.

Scene 10 — The Return (13.5–15 s)

Close on her eyes opening; reflection of inverted skyline within pupils.
Curtains sway with lingering dream wind.
Audio: single crystalline chime, then soft city ambience.
Mood: awakening, transcendence.

